# Durable Go caches

Cursor sandboxes set `GOCACHE` to `/tmp/cursor-sandbox-cache/<session>/`, which is wiped every run. Do not call the system `go` with that value left in the environment.

- Prefer `make test`, `make dae`, or `make print-go-env`.
- For a raw `go` command, prepend repo `hack/bin` or source env first:

```bash
export PATH="$PWD/hack/bin:$PATH"
# or
. hack/env.sh
go test -tags dae_stub_ebpf ./...
```

Never set `GOCACHE` under `/tmp` or `cursor-sandbox-cache`. Machine defaults are `$HOME/go-cache` and `$HOME/go-mod`.
